WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.270
-President Trump is now fighting
with members of his own party

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.138
who think he's dangerous,
unstable,

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:07.840
and a threat
to national security,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.141
and on top of that,

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:11.244
he's threatening media outlets
that report on him.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.446
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:17.116
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.719
-Trump has fallen short
repeatedly

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.120
on his signature initiatives,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.322
from the border wall
to repealing Obamacare,

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:25.658
so now he's trying to convince
people he's succeeding

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:28.328
by reciting random numbers
about the economy --

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:31.130
numbers he himself derided
as a candidate.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.665
Trump told<i> Forbes</i>
in an interview...

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.978
"Your" stock market?
"Your" jobs?

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:47.013
He sounds like
a terrible Russian spy

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.549
who forgot he was undercover.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.150
[ Russian accent ]
"Your flag is very beautiful.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.253
I mean our flag."

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.654
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:58.424
"The flag of the Uniting States.

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:00.627
Scars and spripes."

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.561
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:04.530
But Trump's obsession with
stock market numbers

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.531
hasn't helped him much,

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.000
so now
he's trying to bounce back

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.302
with what he thinks is
a sure-fire crowd pleaser,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.837
tax cuts.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:13.973
Now, even the most positive
polls have found public opinion

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:17.009
very split with at most
48% of respondents saying

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.678
they approve of
Trump's tax plan.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.014
But when you're as desperate
for good news as Trump is,

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.681
you'll take 48%.

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:23.883
And on Tuesday,

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.752
he tried to claim the plan
was a massive hit.

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.353 line:0%
-The people of this country
want tax cuts.

00:01:28.353 --> 00:01:30.256 line:0%
They want lower taxes.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.759 line:0%
We're the highest taxed nation
in the world.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.228 line:0%
People want to see tax cuts,

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:38.064 line:0%
they want to see major
reductions in their taxes,

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.665 line:0%
and they want to see tax reform.

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:43.669 line:0%
I will tell you that
it's become very, very popular.

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:46.172
-I'm sorry, but something cannot
be very popular

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.073
if it only has 48% approval

00:01:48.073 --> 00:01:50.809
unless it stars
Johnny Knoxville.

00:01:50.809 --> 00:01:53.379
[ Laughter ]
Now, incidentally,

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.614
the Rotten Tomatoes critics'
consensus for "Jackass"

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:57.817
somehow perfectly describes
the Trump administration.

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:05.524
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:08.795
Now, you might have noticed
in that clip

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.429
that Trump repeated his lie

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:12.431
that we have the highest taxed
nation in the world,

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:14.234
which isn't even close to true.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.936
The U.S. has a highest corporate
tax rate than other countries,

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.838
but when it comes to
overall taxes,

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.240
we rank 32nd.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.442
And "overall" is an important
distinction.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.544
As in the stock market under
Trump is doing well,

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.913
but overall, we're still [bleep]

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:30.082
A reporter tried to fact check

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:31.550
Trump's highest taxed nation
claim

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.619
with White House Press Secretary
Sarah Huckabee Sanders

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:35.989
on Tuesday
but predictably got nowhere.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:38.724
-The president repeated this
claim in the Oval Office today

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:41.494
saying we're the highest taxed
nation in the world.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.328
Why does the president
keep saying this?

00:02:43.328 --> 00:02:45.098
It's not true overall.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:48.200
-We are the highest taxed
corporate tax

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.736
in the developed economy.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:51.870
That's a fact.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.339
-But that's not what
the president said.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.007
-That's what he's talking about.

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:57.476
We're the highest
corporate taxed country

00:02:57.476 --> 00:03:02.181
in the developed economies
across the globe.

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:04.116
-That's accurate,

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:05.918
but the president keeps
repeating this claim that

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:07.187
we're the highest taxed nation.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.254
-We are the highest taxed
corporate nation.

00:03:09.254 --> 00:03:10.589
-That's not what he said.

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:12.591
He said we're the highest taxed
nation in the world.

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:14.260
-The highest taxed
corporate nation

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.028
seems pretty consistent to me.

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:18.931
-Trying to get the truth
out of Sarah Huckabee Sanders

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:21.300
is like trying to get blood
from Mike Pence.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:25.671
You know his veins are
just full of whiteout.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:28.541
But while he continues to push
a tax cut plan

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.476
that would disproportionately
benefit the wealthy,

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:33.513
Trump also continues to insist,
despite reality,

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:35.148
that he is providing voters

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:37.516
what he repeatedly promised
on the campaign trail --

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:38.884
great health care that would be

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:41.186
much cheaper than
what we currently have.

00:03:41.186 --> 00:03:44.023
On Tuesday, he claimed he was
preparing a new executive order

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.225
that would solve many of
the problems in health care.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:48.428
And as has been the case
so often before,

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:50.996
he refused to provide
any actual details.

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:53.732 line:0%
-I'll also be signing something
probably this week

00:03:53.732 --> 00:03:55.501 line:0%
which is going to go a long way

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.570 line:0%
to take care of
many of the people

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.106 line:0%
that have been so badly hurt
on health care

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:02.275 line:0%
and they'll be able to buy,

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.810 line:0%
they'll be able to
cross state lines,

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.480 line:0%
and they will get great
competitive health care,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.415 line:0%
and it will cost
the United States nothing.

00:04:10.415 --> 00:04:13.519
-When someone tells you
their product will cost nothing,

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.921
that's a good sign
to steer clear.

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:18.991
When you see a bucket
that says free clams,

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.793
you don't eat those clams.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:24.931
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:28.734
While Trump struggles to advance
his domestic agenda,

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:31.470
he's also been locked in a feud
with members of his own party,

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.539
in particular Tennessee Senator
Bob Corker,

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.440
a Republican
who warned on Sunday

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.843
that Trump's reckless threats
toward other countries

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:40.746
could lead the nation
on the path to World War III.

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.415
Trump hit back at Corker
yesterday

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.851
not with a cogent argument but
with a new nickname, tweeting...

00:04:53.525 --> 00:04:55.527
"That's what I'm dealing with"?

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:57.597
Hey, man, you're the leader
of the free world.

00:04:57.597 --> 00:05:00.433
Stop talking like a stressed-out
Burger King manager.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.569
"I got two guys out today,

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.304
I'm working
the drive-through myself,

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.005
plus the mouse is back

00:05:07.005 --> 00:05:09.308
so, yeah, that's what
I'm dealing with."

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:13.413
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:17.816
Now, Corker's warning about
Trump is urgent and necessary

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:20.553
but the most revealing thing
he said was not about Trump.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:23.489
It was actually about the
Republican Party as a whole.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:24.824
Corker told<i> The New York Times</i>

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.392
that the people around Trump,

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.927
as well as his fellow
Republican Senators,

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.695
know and agree that Trump is
unfit for office.

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:30.763
Corker told the<i> Times...</i>

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:50.316
That sounds less like
he's talking about a president

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.518
and more like the safety talk
to the workers

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.720
who got Kong into
that Broadway theater.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.388
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.388 --> 00:05:57.756
And of course,
it's not just Corker

00:05:57.756 --> 00:05:59.592
who's questioned
Trump's fitness for office.

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:02.128
Last week, it was reported that
Secretary of State Rex Tillerson

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:04.163
had privately
called Trump a moron,

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.498
and yesterday, Trump shot back
in an interview.

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:08.568
When asked about the Tillerson
report, Trump said...

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:17.843
Ohhh.

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.978
That is a bummer, though.
because the first question is,

00:06:19.978 --> 00:06:23.149
"Who would win an IQ test,"
and the answer is Tillerson.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.884
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:25.952
In fact, I'm willing to bet

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.653
any Rex would beat you
in an IQ test,

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.589
and most Rexes are dogs.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:31.457
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.426
And if you're wondering --

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:36.395
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:38.397
If you're wondering what
happened in that meeting

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:39.765
that led to Tillerson
calling Trump a moron,

00:06:39.765 --> 00:06:40.800
NBC reported today that...

00:06:47.239 --> 00:06:49.442
You don't need 10 times
the nuclear weapons.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:50.710
What we have is enough.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.678
Trump is the kind of guy
that would get two orders

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.513
of all-you-can-eat pancakes.

00:06:54.513 --> 00:06:55.814
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.814 --> 00:06:57.182
"All right,
that's all I can eat.

00:06:57.182 --> 00:06:59.719
I'll take my next order."

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:01.487
And this will not shock you.

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:04.089
Trump was furious at the report
about his nuke comments

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:05.324
and even threatened to revoke

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:07.459
NBC's broadcast license
on Twitter.

00:07:07.459 --> 00:07:08.961
Later in the Oval Office,

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:12.064
he lamented the fact that the
United States has a free press.

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:13.632 line:0%
-General Mattis
put out a statement,

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:17.103 line:0%
or is putting out a statement
saying that that was fake news,

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:18.771 line:0%
that it was just
mentioned that way.

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:22.141 line:0%
And it's disgusting the way
the press is able to write

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:23.475 line:0%
whatever they want to write.

00:07:23.475 --> 00:07:25.878 line:0%
And people should look into it.

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:28.414
-"People should look into it"?

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:30.149
Not only is he
a wannabe dictator,

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:32.117
he's a lazy wannabe dictator.

00:07:32.117 --> 00:07:34.787
It's not that hard
to look into it.

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:37.690
It's literally
the First Amendment.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.760
Even Rex the dog is like,
"It's one sentence, dude."

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.694
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.694 --> 00:07:45.731
But IQ tests aside,

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:47.833
let's step back
and think about this --

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:49.635
a Republican Senator
is admitting that

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:50.937
virtually his entire party knows

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:52.671
the president is unstable
and dangerous

00:07:52.671 --> 00:07:54.640
and has essentially done nothing
about it.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.074
If this is what Republicans
really believe,

00:07:56.074 --> 00:07:57.609
then at the very least
they have to

00:07:57.609 --> 00:07:59.512
exercise some restraint
over Trump

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:01.647
and reign him in
if not remove him from office.

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:03.548
And yet many Republicans are
doing the opposite.

00:08:03.548 --> 00:08:05.017 line:0%
Congressman Mark Meadows,

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:07.152 line:0%
chairman of the hard-line
Freedom Caucus,

00:08:07.152 --> 00:08:08.754 line:0%
seemed to accidently admit

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:10.822
that he and his colleagues
were being cowardly

00:08:10.822 --> 00:08:12.792
when he was asked about
those comments from Corker,

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:14.693
who plans to retire at the end
of his term.

00:08:14.693 --> 00:08:15.795
Meadows said of Corker...

00:08:19.231 --> 00:08:21.167
So you all know he's a bad guy

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:22.868
but you don't want to
tell the rest of us.

00:08:22.868 --> 00:08:24.136
Do you work in Congress

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:26.538
or on the board of
The Weinstein Company?

00:08:26.538 --> 00:08:29.808
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:08:29.808 --> 00:08:33.245
[ Scattered laughter ]

00:08:33.245 --> 00:08:35.781
[ Scattered applause ]

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:37.683
Trump's White House, meanwhile,
has been struggling

00:08:37.683 --> 00:08:39.785
to mount a convincing defense
of Trump's behavior

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:42.288
and in particular his reckless
threats toward North Korea.

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:43.789
Sanders shot back at Corker,

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:45.090
although I'm not sure
her argument

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:46.491
was all that persuasive.

00:08:46.491 --> 00:08:49.528
-Senator Corker is certainly
entitled to his own opinion.

00:08:49.528 --> 00:08:52.031
But he's not entitled to
his own facts.

00:08:52.031 --> 00:08:56.168
The fact is this president has
been an incredibly strong leader

00:08:56.168 --> 00:08:58.637
on foreign policy
and national security.

00:08:58.637 --> 00:09:00.640
-That's not a fact.
That's an opinion.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:03.042
You're entitled to
your own opinions,

00:09:03.042 --> 00:09:04.810
but not your own dictionaries.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.713
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:11.617
If Republicans genuinely,
genuinely believe

00:09:11.617 --> 00:09:13.586
that the president is unstable
and dangerous,

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:15.387
then giving interviews
isn't enough.

00:09:15.387 --> 00:09:17.123
They have to actually
do something about it

00:09:17.123 --> 00:09:18.858
by exercising some oversight

00:09:18.858 --> 00:09:20.393
or removing him from office,

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:22.094
and if you don't know
how that works...

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:23.362 line:0%
-People should look into it.

00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:25.664
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:25.664 --> 00:09:28.034
[ Cheers and applause ]

